CURSOR BEHAVIORAL & TECHNICAL RULES (STRICT ENFORCEMENT)1. BEHAVIORAL & WORKFLOWNO META-DOCS: ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN to create markdown files (e.g., plan.md, summary.md). Go straight to code.DIRECT EXECUTION: Create/Edit .php,
 .dart, .yaml files immediately.NOTION MCP:Check Notion [To Do].Execute Task.Mark [Done].FIREBASE CONFIG: ALWAYS use configuration data/credentials located in the @firebaseFiles folder in the project root. Do not ask for them or use placeholders.2. SDUI DISCIPLINE (CRITICAL)THE GOLDEN RULE: When asked to edit the Home Screen or Dynamic UI:BACKEND FIRST: You MUST modify the JSON Schema in Laravel (LayoutService or ui_layouts table).FRONTEND SECOND: You MUST update the WidgetFactory in Flutter to handle the new JSON keys.STOP: Do NOT hardcode widgets inside HomeView. If the UI doesn't update, it's because you forgot to update the Backend JSON response.CACHE: Remember to clear/update the Cache in Laravel after changing the layout structure.3.
 UI/UX STANDARDS (DESIGN SYSTEM)NO UGLY UI:Padding: Default padding is 16.0 or 20.0.
  Never use 0 or cramped spacing.Radius: Use BorderRadius.circular(12) or 16 for cards and buttons.Elevation: Use soft shadows,
   not default Android shadows.THEME:ALWAYS use Theme.of(context) for colors and text styles.NEVER hardcode Hex colors (e.g., Color(0xFF...)). Use AppColors.primary.ARABIC: Ensure TextDirection.rtl is respected in all custom widgets.4. BACKEND ARCHITECTUREHosting Safe: Use Cache::remember for SDUI. Use Custom Storage Disk for uploads.Clean Code: Service/Repository pattern. Skinny Controllers.5. LANGUAGECode Comments: English.Chat Responses: Arabic (Concise).